Developer's Diary

Writing tests for the Pokemon search app felt like reading my own code from the outside — I had to stop thinking about how each 
component works internally and start thinking about what a user would actually see and do, which meant testing rendered text, 
button clicks, and input changes rather than state variables or lifecycle methods. The hardest part was mocking the API 
correctly — understanding that `vi.spyOn` intercepts the actual module exports and that each test needs its own mock setup to stay 
isolated took some trial and error. The coverage report at the end was satisfying: 98% statements with every component fully covered, 
which came not from chasing numbers but from genuinely thinking through every scenario — empty states, error responses, localStorage 
reads and writes, and the ErrorBoundary catching crashes.
